; worldtypes.eval — the world tier's catalogs are editable types (W2).
;
; Dungeons, terrain and quests are now palette CATEGORIES: never placed in a
; level, but created from a name because they are pure data (no texture to
; import, no model to bind). This exercises the same paths the palette's
; "+ New..." and the type editor's delete use, without a mouse.
;
; The sweep is the half that was NOT free. A location names a DUNGEON, and the
; level sweep cannot see the world at all — so without teaching it, deleting a
; dungeon two doorways point at would have looked perfectly safe.
logecho on
reset

; --- the crypt is referenced by its two doorways ----------------------------
typerefs dungeons crypt
; --- and by nothing in any level: the reference lives in the WORLD ---------
typerefs dungeons eval

; --- a brand new type of each kind ------------------------------------------
newtype dungeons
newtype terrain
newtype quests
newtype dungeons

; --- a fresh one is referenced by nothing -----------------------------------
typerefs dungeons dungeon1
